Subject: [PATCH] Skip idle XPSTTS polling loops in whole loop periods

Games wait for the VIP by reading XPSTTS in a tight loop: Virtual Boy
Wario Land read it 87 million times in 3000 frames, about 17 % of a
Cortex-A7's time (Powkiddy A12/A13). When the same instruction reads the
same value again, with every program register as before and no memory
written in between, the loop has no effect but time. Advance the clock by
whole loop periods, staying before the next event and before XPSTTS's
SBOUT bit can change, so the loop reads the same values at the same cycle
phase as it would have. The remembered poll is dropped when timestamps are
rebased each frame, on power and on state load. The registers are
compared, through an inline accessor, only after the cheap checks pass. Output is bit-identical
(frame hashes of five games, two anaglyph presets); Wario Land skips 63
million of its loop iterations.

diff --git a/mednafen/vb/vip.c b/mednafen/vb/vip.c
index 229351c..8039308 100644
--- a/mednafen/vb/vip.c
+++ b/mednafen/vb/vip.c
@@ -704,6 +704,13 @@ uint8 VIP_Read8(int32 timestamp, uint32 A)
    return 0;
 }
 
+/* The latest timestamp up to which XPSTTS cannot change without an event:
+ * its SBOUT bit flips at SBOUT_InactiveTime (idle-loop skip, libretro.cpp). */
+int32 VIP_PollLimit(int32 timestamp)
+{
+   return timestamp < SBOUT_InactiveTime ? SBOUT_InactiveTime : INT32_MAX;
+}
+
 uint16 VIP_Read16(int32 timestamp, uint32 A)
 {
    switch(A >> 16)
